```
$ gen-circleci-orb ensure-orb-registered --help
Ensure a CircleCI orb is registered, creating it if it does not exist.

A small CI-internal helper (not something a consumer normally runs by hand): the generated orb-release workflow calls this before `orb-tools/publish` so the very first publish of a brand-new orb namespace/name doesn't fail on a missing orb. Idempotent — a no-op once the orb already exists.

Usage: gen-circleci-orb ensure-orb-registered [OPTIONS] --orb-name <ORB_NAME>

Options:
      --orb-name <ORB_NAME>
          The orb name to check/register (e.g. my-org/my-orb)

      --private
          Register the orb as private when creating it.
          
          Must be set correctly on first creation — orb visibility cannot be changed after the orb is created.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
